---
title: Lemon-Artichoke Skillet Chicken Thighs
course: main
cuisine: mediterranean
servings: 3
time_active: 20
time_total: 45
leftovers: good
tags: [weeknight, one-pot]
pairs: [roasted-asparagus]
description: Crisp-skinned thighs finished in the oven over a lemony artichoke pan sauce.
---

Heat the oven to 400°F. Pat @chicken thighs{1.5%lb}(bone-in, skin-on, 4-5 pieces) very dry and season all over with @salt and @black pepper{}.

Heat @olive oil{1%tbsp} in a large #oven-safe skillet{} over medium-high. Lay the thighs in skin-side down and leave them alone until the skin is deep golden and crisp, ~{6-8%minutes}. Flip, sear 1 minute more, and move to a plate.

Pour off all but about 1 tbsp of fat and lower the heat to medium. Add @shallot{1}(thinly sliced) and @garlic{3%clove}(thinly sliced) and cook until soft, ~{2%minutes}.

Pour in @white wine{1/2%cup}(or more broth) and scrape up the browned bits. Simmer until reduced by half, ~{2%minutes}.

Stir in @chicken broth{1/2%cup}, @artichoke hearts{1%can}(14 oz, drained and quartered), @dried oregano{1/2%tsp}, and the zest of a @lemon{1}. Bring to a simmer.

Nestle the thighs back in skin-side up, keeping the skin above the liquid. Roast until the chicken reaches 175°F, ~{20-25%minutes}. Put the asparagus in on another rack for the last 15 minutes.

Move the chicken to a plate. Set the skillet over medium (the handle is hot) and swirl in @butter{2%tbsp} and the juice of the lemon. Simmer until glossy, ~{1-2%minutes}, then taste for salt.

Spoon the sauce and artichokes around the chicken, not over it, so the skin stays crisp. Scatter with @?parsley{}(chopped).

> Boneless, skinless thighs work too: sear 4 minutes a side and roast only 10-12 minutes. Crusty bread or orzo soaks up the sauce. Leftovers keep 3 days; the skin softens but the sauce is still good.
